1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
[sighs]

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
What now, Zaikahal?

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

4
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
[singer singing in English]

5
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

6
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
[singer singing in English]

7
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
[singer singing in English]

8
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
EVIL X AND X TERRIBLE

10
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,000
[narrator] His name is Gyro,
the NGL's shadow don.

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
[narrator] Gyro spent
the first 12 years of his life

12
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,000
until Gyro finally killed him
and made his escape.

13
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
It was incredibly rare
for him to talk to Gyro,

14
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
who slept on the upper bunk.

15
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
It was for that reason

16
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
he barely knew how to speak
before he was seven years old.

17
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:01,000
When Gyro returned from work,
he was not permitted to leave his bed,

18
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
and only before 9:00 p.m.

19
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
The rotting wood of the bed frame
would creak loudly

20
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
whenever he would turn in his sleep.

21
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
-[creaking]
-[narrator] His father hated that sound.

22
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Once, that noise caused his father
to beat him severely,

23
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:33,000
and after that, Gyro learned to sleep
without moving a muscle.

24
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
He also learned
to hold his bladder at night

25
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
and kept an empty liquor bottle
by his bedside

26
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,000
for when he simply
couldn't hold it in any longer.

27
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
learning from his mistakes.

28
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:10,000
His father had never bought him anything,
not even a toy,

29
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Inside his small, troubled world,
his father was essentially a god,

30
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
and no matter how cruel
his father could be,

31
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Gyro continued to idolize the man,

32
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
believing that deep down,
his father truly needed him,

33
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
a belief stemming from two facts.

34
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
When Gyro was five,

35
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,000
he suffered a terrible fever
that nearly killed him.

36
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,000
His father stayed up all night,
replacing his towels with fresh ones.

37
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:55,000
The other reason was that his father had
never at any point ordered him to leave,

38
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
not even once.

39
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:03,000
And these two facts
filled Gyro's young heart with pride.

40
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
You idiot!

41
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
You know why your dad
hasn't kicked you out yet?

42
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
It's just because
you still bring in money.

43
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
[narrator] Though he had
previously kept that possibility

44
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
locked away deep in his mind,

45
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
when the older youth
brought it to light so harshly,

46
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
something in Gyro snapped.

47
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
His pride gravely wounded,
a feeling of rage overcame him,

48
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
and he attacked the youth.

49
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,000
[spoon clatters]

50
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:47,000
to the point where not even
knocking Gyro out would satisfy him.

51
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
He stomped on the boy's face, spat on him,

52
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:56,000
and then he uttered the finishing blow.

53
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
When you got sick,
it was a neighbor who took care of you!

54
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Bet you didn't know that, did you?

55
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Your dad didn't lift a finger for you.

56
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:20,000
He asked your dad
what he would do if his kid died,

57
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
and do you wanna know what he said?

58
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:30,000
It wouldn't matter.
I don't care if he lives or if he dies.

59
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
That was when Gyro finally understood.

60
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
-[drink pouring]
-No one cares if I live or die,

61
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
not even my own father.

62
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:17,000
In other words, my life has no meaning.

63
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
if I live, I'll bring in money.

64
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:26,000
if I die, I'll free up space in the room.
That's all.

65
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
but I know now
that the only reason he said that

66
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,000
was so he could avoid
any inconvenience for himself.

67
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Those words
were never meant to help his son.

68
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
'Others' meant my father.

69
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
No.

70
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
It meant 'humans.'

71
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Eventually the boy stood up,

72
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
and he grabbed a nearby hammer.

73
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Nine years later, Gyro founded the NGL,

74
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
which became a nation
nine years after that

75
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
with him as its king.

76
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:45,000
The drug DD was merely the first step
in achieving that greater goal.

77
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,000
[scoffs] I didn't feel like fighting them.

78
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
The food will reach the Queen either way.

79
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Gyro, huh?

80
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Damn it. I should have just eaten him.

81
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Listen up. I'm taking over this factory.

82
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
From now on, this is my fortress!

83
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
-[gunshot]
-[birds screeching]

84
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
[gunshots]

85
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
[laughing]

86
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
[gunshots and laughter echoing]

87
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Hang on.
Exactly what the hell is going on here?

88
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Actually, one of my own
has gone totally missing too.

89
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Its communications have been cut off,
and it hasn't returned yet.

90
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Yunju's team
dealt with all the humans holding guns.

91
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Now, how would I know that?

92
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Probably some brand-new weapon
that we haven't seen yet.

93
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:33,000
I can tell because the bullets
are still lodged inside of the body.

94
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I'm not so sure about the others.

95
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
It appears the skull was punctured.

96
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:56,000
It said one human mimicked firing a gun,
and although no projectile emerged,

97
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:00,000
something pierced the soldiers' skulls,
killing them.

98
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,000
So they possess
a number of abilities we do not.

99
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
These humans
may be tougher than we thought.

100
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,000
[scoffs] If it's a human power,
then I'm sure we can learn to use it,

101
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,000
since we've inherited those traits.
It's not a big deal.

102
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,000
You don't understand.

103
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
The humans' real strength
lies in their ability to learn things.

104
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Yes, I suppose you do have a point there.

105
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Who in the world is Reina?

106
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Uh, I didn't say it. You did.

107
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
that are capable of defeating
our foot soldiers.

108
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:31,000
[sighs] What do we do?

109
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Only soldiers of our rank
can use complex weapons,

110
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,000
but humans are fortunately
not aware of that fact.

111
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
That will definitely frighten them.

112
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
[Peggy] I see.

113
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Reina, huh?

114
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
[bees buzzing]

115
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[Ponzu] It's no use.
No one received the message.

116
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:18,000
So the other Hunters we were
in contact with are probably dead.

117
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,000
I see.

118
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Let's go.

119
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Those creatures are too much
for us to handle.

120
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
We need to get out of the NGL

121
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
and tell the whole world
what's happening here,

122
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
then form an extermination team.

123
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Fine! Whatever!
Let's just hurry up and get out of here…

124
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,000
[sighs]

125
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,000
[body thudding]

126
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
[gasps] It's…

127
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Come on! More will be coming soon.

128
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,000
-[Pike] Hold on.
-[all gasp]

129
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,000
I thought I instructed you
to capture the humans alive, didn't I?

130
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
We're supposed to deliver them
to the Queen while they're fresh.

131
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Wait. That's a human face.

132
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
But what is that thing?

133
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
[Balda] Fire! Open fire!

134
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
ORANGE ARROW

135
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
[Pokkle] My Orange Arrow is the fastest
of my Seven Spectrum Array Rainbows,

136
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
and he caught it easily.

137
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[Balda screaming]

138
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Balda!

139
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,000
[Balda screams]

140
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
You bastard!

141
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Wait. One moment, please.
My hands are full.

142
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:04,000
You're pathetic in battle,
but that's hardly unusual.

143
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
the nutritional value
of a thousand normal humans.

144
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Well done, Pike. Good job.

145
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,000
[Pike swoons]

146
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
[gasps] Mistress Zazan!

147
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:37,000
I am ever so grateful for your praise.
You honor me.

148
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
[Ponzu] I can't save him myself.
I have to call for help.

149
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
There might still be time.

150
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Even if they take him,
they probably won't eat him right away.

151
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Please, take this to the Hunter
with the strongest aura you can find.

152
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
I have to get back to the border
as fast as I can.

153
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
This is so much fun.

154
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
[chomping]

155
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Hunting is so much fun.

156
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
HELP!

157
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
CHIMERA ANT NEST

158
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
ROCKY AREA

159
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,000
NOTIFY HUNTER ASSOCIATION!

160
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
-[Kite] It'll be risky.
-[boys gasp]

161
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
You sure you want to come along?

162
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Yeah.

163
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
We're professionals, aren't we?

164
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Miss translator,
I'm sorry, but we really must hurry.

165
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Right.

166
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:54,000
I'm sure the horses can gallop
a bit faster if it's necessary.

167
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
-They still won't be fast enough.
-Huh?

168
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:01,000
I want you two to return to the border
and rendezvous with the others.

169
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Then call the Association.

170
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
These things are dangerous.

171
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Got it.

172
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
You be careful, okay, Kite?

173
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,000
I will.

174
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Keep up, or I'll leave you behind.

175
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Yep, and right back at you.

176
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Let's go.

177
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,000
[stammers]

178
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
This is a bullet casing.

179
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:05,000
But I thought anything mechanical
was forbidden here, isn't it?

180
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:09,000
It means the underground rulers of the NGL

181
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:12,000
weren't only manufacturing drugs,
but weapons.

182
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Yeah, but judging by this…

183
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
[Kite] This wasn't a human.

184
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Most likely, it was a Chimera Ant.

185
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
If my instincts are correct

186
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,000
and the Chimera Ants
are using firearms now…

187
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,000
I hate to say it,

188
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:36,000
but it's possible
the NGL's underground rulers

189
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,000
have already been fed to the Queen.

190
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:44,000
What would happen if the Chimera Ants
were born with their genes?

191
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
The NGL and the Chimera Ants,

192
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,000
it's the worst combination imaginable.

193
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,000
This will be an unprecedented biohazard.

194
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:07,000
[narrator] The situation has taken
a sudden turn for the absolute worst.

195
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,000
[closing theme music playing]

196
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

197
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,000
[upbeat music playing]

198
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:37,000
[Gon] Next time, "The Fight Begins."

199
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:40,000
Ready, set, Gon!

200
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,000
[grunts]
